        <qualifiedname>csmp::JaggedArray3D_Comparison_Test::ComparePerformanceWithVectorOfVectors</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_test" kindref="compound">Test</ref> Parameters: • The test creates both Jagged3DArray and <ref refid="classvector" kindref="compound">vector&lt;vector&lt;vector&lt;double&gt;&gt;&gt;</ref> structures with dimensions 6x4x3 and populates them with sequential values starting from 1.0.<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Random Access: • A loop performs 1,000,000 random accesses to elements in both structures. • Random indices are generated using mt19937 and uniform_int_distribution.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Timing: • The chrono::high_resolution_clock is used to measure the duration of the random access for both structures.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Volatile Keyword: • The volatile keyword is used to prevent the compiler from optimizing away the loop by assuming the results are unused.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Output: • The program prints the time taken (in microseconds) for both the vector and Jagged3DArray. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
